From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer, winex11: End task ends a hung Linux program

Task Manager's End task on a Linux program asked it to close (WM_CLOSE to
its frame or stand-in: WM_DELETE_WINDOW / XCLOSE). A hung one never answers:
CPU-X hung and could not be ended (David 2026-10-02). As Windows ends a
program that does not answer, the frame or stand-in now answers the
registered message SgLinuxWindowEnd (Task Manager sends it when the program
did not close): a framed program's process -- the one its window names,
_NET_WM_PID; kill() refuses another user's -- is killed and its X connection
closed (winex11); an unframed one is killed by the compositor (XKILL,
sg-compositor 0.2.0+sg28, the asking user's own only).

Gates: test/linuxembed-gate.sh (a stopped xterm; mutant
SG_MUTANT_END_TASK_POLITE), test/linuxstandin-gate.sh (XKILL; mutant
SG_MUTANT_END_TASK_IGNORED).
---
--- a/programs/explorer/systray.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/systray.c
@@ -1622,8 +1622,22 @@
 
 static LRESULT CALLBACK sg_linux_standin_proc( HWND hwnd, UINT msg, WPARAM wp, LPARAM lp )
 {
+    static UINT end_msg;
     struct taskbar_button *win;
 
+    /* Task Manager's End task, when the program did not close when asked: it
+     * is ended (its process killed), as Windows ends a program that does not
+     * answer -- a hung Linux program could not be ended (David 2026-10-02) */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_END_TASK_IGNORED
+    if (!end_msg) end_msg = RegisterWindowMessageW( L"SgLinuxWindowEnd" );
+    if (msg == end_msg && (win = find_taskbar_button( hwnd )))
+    {
+        if (win->embedded) sg_embed_call( hwnd, SG_EMBED_CLOSE, 1 );
+        else sg_xwin_command( win, L"XKILL" );
+        return 0;
+    }
+#endif
+
     /* a frame for a program that draws its own title bar and edges (SG
      * Office, Firefox): no title bar or border of ours, the program's window
      * fills it; it is sizable (WS_THICKFRAME) only so it maximizes to the
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/sg_embed.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/sg_embed.c
@@ -50,7 +50,9 @@
 #include "config.h"
 
 #include <pthread.h>
+#include <signal.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
 #include <X11/Xlib.h>
 #include <X11/Xutil.h>
 #include <X11/Xatom.h>
@@ -801,6 +803,20 @@
         int i, n;
         BOOL polite = FALSE;
         X11DRV_expect_error( display, ignore_error, NULL );
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_END_TASK_POLITE
+        if (wp == 1)
+        {
+            /* End task on a program that did not close when asked (a hung
+             * one: CPU-X, David 2026-10-02): its process ended -- the one
+             * its window names (_NET_WM_PID; kill() refuses another user's)
+             * -- and its X connection closed */
+            long pid = get_cardinal( display, child, XInternAtom( display, "_NET_WM_PID", False ) );
+            if (pid > 1 && pid != getpid()) kill( pid, SIGKILL );
+            XKillClient( display, child );
+            X11DRV_check_error();
+            return 0;
+        }
+#endif
         if (XGetWMProtocols( display, child, &protocols, &n ))
         {
             for (i = 0; i < n; i++) if (protocols[i] == x11drv_atom(WM_DELETE_WINDOW)) polite = TRUE;
